**deadzone.hpp applies validated radial deadzones to gamepad aim stick vectors.**

## Interface

- `deadzone_params` stores `magnitude inner`, `magnitude outer`, and `magnitude anti`, defaulting to `0.0f`.
- `validate(const deadzone_params&, string& why) noexcept` returns `bool`, enforcing each value in `[0, 1)` and `inner < 1 - outer`; failures write a specific reason.
- `apply(const deadzone_params&, stick_vector) noexcept` returns `stick_vector`, assuming validated params and asserting the invariant.

## Behavior & Dependencies

`apply` maps magnitude to zero through `inner`, linearly to one at `1 - outer`, clamps beyond saturation, applies `anti` after non-zero output, and preserves direction exactly. `types.hpp` supplies `magnitude`, `string`, and controller types; `utility.hpp`, `aim/types.hpp`, and `sample/axis.hpp` supply supporting utilities and `stick_vector`.